steps.do:
For each issue, check before filing:
(1) the disputed amount is at least $1.00;
(2) the transaction is no more than 60 days old, counted from its date (i_match) to today (v_time);
(3) the linked account is OPEN (a_accounts).
If any check fails, tell the customer this transaction cannot be disputed and why, and do not file it.

Tell the customer three things:
- Rho-Bank submits a chargeback request to the ATM owner/network;
- the investigation can take up to 90 days;
- provisional credit is still required within 10 business days.

Tell the customer four things:
- an Electronic Fund Transfer Error Resolution Affidavit will be emailed to their registered email;
- they have 10 business days to sign and return it;
- not returning it may lead to denial of the claim;
- signing a false affidavit is a federal offense.

For each dispute, check the four required conditions:
(1) reported within 60 days of the statement date showing the transaction (true for a transaction that passed c_prefiling; see lb_liability);
(2) the category is unauthorized_transaction, card_present_fraud, card_not_present_fraud, atm_cash_discrepancy or duplicate_charge;
(3) the written statement was provided (w_statement);
(4) the account is OPEN with no holds or restrictions (a_accounts).
If all four hold, provisional credit is required: set provisional_credit_eligible = true.
A 'not required' case may also apply: merchant not contacted for a non-fraud dispute, pin_compromised = yes_shared, or an account under 30 days old with a card-not-present transaction. That passage still allows credit ('may be offered at discretion'), so true meets both passages.
If any of the four fails, set it to false. This includes goods_services_not_received, recurring_charge_after_cancellation, atm_deposit_not_credited and incorrect_amount. Credit is then not required, though it may be offered at discretion.

Confirm each filed dispute to the customer:
- its category;
- whether provisional credit applies: the full disputed amount, reduced by the $50 or $500 liability if they reported late, and issued within 10 business days of filing (20 for accounts open less than 30 days);
- the investigation timeline: 45 business days with provisional credit, or 90 days for international transactions, POS outside the US, or new accounts;
- that provisional credit is reversed only after at least 3 business days' written notice;
- any affidavit due.
Name any issue not filed, and why.

First tell the customer four things:
- new transactions will be declined while the card is frozen;
- recurring payments will be declined too;
- pending authorized transactions may still process;
- they can unfreeze it any time through customer service or the mobile app.
Then unlock and call freeze_debit_card_3892. If the card is already FROZEN, nothing more is needed. If it is in any other status, explain that it cannot be frozen.
